                "When international pricing strategies cross the boundary of fair competition, they ignite fierce regulatory, diplomatic, and legal confrontations. In international trade law, few practices carry more severe punitive consequences than Dumping.",
                "Under World Trade Organization (WTO) definitions, Dumping occurs when an enterprise exports a product to a foreign market at a price below its 'Normal Value'. Normal value is legally defined as: (a) The price charged for the identical product in the exporter's domestic home market; or (b) In the absence of domestic sales, the fully-loaded cost of production plus reasonable selling expenses and operating profit.",
