                "3. Persistent Dumping: Continuous international price discrimination, where an enterprise exploits differing price elasticities across nations—charging high monopoly prices in a protected domestic market while selling at low marginal cost in competitive foreign markets.",
                "WTO Anti-Dumping Remedies: Under Article VI of GATT 1994 (The Anti-Dumping Agreement), an importing nation is legally authorized to impose punitive Anti-Dumping Duties (ADD) on foreign imports if it satisfies three strict evidentiary criteria through an official investigation: (1) Proof of Dumping (export price is empirically below normal value); (2) Proof of Material Economic Injury (domestic manufacturers suffered significant declines in sales, market share, profits, or employment); and (3) A Direct Causal Link proving dumped imports caused the injury.",
